Make the keymapper overlay actually go fullscreen.

setup_window() is commented "Set fullscreen" but calls self.maximize(), which a
tiling compositor ignores -- Hyprland tiles the window into free space instead
of honouring a maximise request, so the overlay keeps a corner-sized
allocation (observed 441x705 over a 2625x1410 Android surface).
waydroid-helper#106.

set_fullscreen() is an explicit request the compositor honours regardless of
tiling, which is also what the widget coordinates are scaled against --
do_size_allocate() records the resulting allocation as host_resolution.

--- a/waydroid_helper/controller/app/window.py
+++ b/waydroid_helper/controller/app/window.py
@@ -473,7 +473,7 @@
         """Sets window properties"""
         self.realize()
         self.set_decorated(False)
-        self.maximize()
+        self.fullscreen()

         self.set_name("transparent-window")
